# Environment files. Every one of them is ignored, .env included: an
# environment file is a local file, not a repo file.
#
# .env was tracked here until 20260827. Nothing secret was ever committed to
# it -- both keys it carried decode to role "anon", the Turnstile key is the
# site key, and the rest is the project ref and URL -- and git history was
# checked across every .env blob in history before it was untracked (114
# commits at the time; two distinct blobs, one anon JWT). This is not
# remediation. It is removing the slot. A tracked .env in a public repository
# is a file the next contributor edits by habit, and the edit that finally
# matters is the one that adds SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY to it.
#
# Names and shapes go in .env.example, which stays tracked and holds no
# values. Values go in .env, .dev.vars, or .env.local on your own machine,
# and in the deployment's environment in production. Server-only secrets --
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, RESEND_API_KEY, TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY -- never
# reach this repository at all.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

